# Master vs Product Folder Layout

**`main`** = MongoDB portfolio demo (v1). **`product`** = PostgreSQL sellable line (v2).

Do not mix v1 and v2 artifacts in the same folder. Mirror the `product/` subfolder pattern everywhere it applies.

## Backend

| Area | v1 (master) | v2 (product branch) |
|------|-------------|------------------------|
| Models | `backend/models/` (e.g. `tea.py`) | `backend/models/product/` |
| Schemas | `backend/schemas/` | `backend/schemas/product/` |
| Tests | `backend/tests/` | `backend/tests/product/` |
| Repositories (future) | — | `backend/repositories/postgres/` |

## Tests

- **v1 tests** — Mongo, `admin`/`user`/`guest`, `tea` routes → `backend/tests/` (`conftest.py`, `test_tea_*.py`, `test_orders_api.py`, …)
- **v2 tests** — deployment, capabilities, PG models/schemas, `owner` only → `backend/tests/product/` (`conftest.py`, `test_deployment.py`, …)

```text
backend/tests/
  conftest.py          # v1 FakeDB, admin/user/guest fixtures
  test_orders_api.py   # v1 Mongo order flow
  product/
    conftest.py        # owner fixtures, personal/professional apps
    test_capabilities.py
    test_models.py
```

## Roles in tests

| Branch | Roles in tests |
|--------|----------------|
| master / v1 tests | `admin`, `user`, `guest` |
| product / v2 tests | `owner` only — never `admin`, `user`, or `guest` |

## Avoid

- Product tests in `backend/tests/test_product_*.py` (use `tests/product/` instead)
- v1 role names in `tests/product/`
- Importing v1 `tea` schemas from product routes or vice versa without an explicit migration path